<===> README.md
`math.pow()` must be as accurate as the Dart VM: the C library `pow` of
MinGW-w64 is often off by one ulp (e.g. for about half of all integer
exponents), which is visible for large results. Exponents 1, 2 and 3 are
computed by multiplication, like the Dart VM does.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> cube/input.scss
@use "sass:math";
a {
  // Like the Dart VM, a power of 3 is computed as x * x * x
  b: math.pow(1291441.0144450965, 3);
}
<===> cube/output.css
a {
  b: 2153891015549136384;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> integer_exponent/input.scss
@use "sass:math";
a {
  b: math.pow(11, 20);
  c: math.pow(11, 25);
  d: math.pow(13, 40);
}
<===> integer_exponent/output.css
a {
  b: 672749994932560100000;
  c: 108347059433883730000000000;
  d: 361188648084531400000000000000000000000000000;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> negative_exponent/input.scss
@use "sass:math";
a {
  b: math.pow(0.3, -15);
  c: math.pow(0.3, -20);
  d: math.pow(-0.000000000001, -2);
}
<===> negative_exponent/output.css
a {
  b: 69691719.37625636;
  c: 28679719907.924435;
  d: 1000000000000000000000000;
}
